## Rules

- Prefer formal numbered assumptions over introduction-level summaries.
- Separate design assumptions, sparsity assumptions, similarity assumptions,
  moment/tail assumptions, and source-selection assumptions.
- Do not force binary labels when a paper has a more nuanced condition.
- Cite source file names for every cell or claim.
- Include `Reliability / Verification status` for each major section.

## Required Structure

1. Paper x assumption matrix
2. Similarity/transfer assumptions
3. Source-target design assumptions
4. Negative-transfer/source-selection assumptions
5. Assumption conflicts and incompatibilities
6. Reliability notes

